.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt PASSWD 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm passwd
.Nd change, lock or unlock a password
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l | Fl u
.Op Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
replaces the
.Pa /etc/shadow
hash for
.Ar name ,
or for the caller when no operand is given.
The new password is prompted twice, hashed with SHA-512-crypt
.Pq Li $6$ ,
and stored with the current last-change day.
.Pp
The
.Fl l
option prefixes the hash with
.Ql ! ;
.Fl u
removes one such marker.
A locked record never authenticates.
.Pp
Root may change every account. Other users may change only their own password after
verifying the old one; that path needs the setuid binary and kernel credentials from U3 and is
not shipped in 0.2.0.
.Pp
The console server echoes input in this release. Echo suppression needs the terminal-mode
work in U3.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/shadow -compact
.It Pa /etc/shadow
password records, mode 0600
.It Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
exclusive update lock
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr useradd 1 ,
.Xr su 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
